{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA257311","title":"Hetrotrophic bacterial community assembly in two pilot and eight full-scale activated sludge wastewater treatment plants","description":"Abstract: Heterotrophic bacterial community assemblies at eight full-scale and two pilot scale activated sludge wastewater treatment plants (AS-WWTPs) were determined by high-throughput pyrosequencing of 16S rRNA gene amplicons. A total of 39 samples covered a range of abiotic factors spread over space and time (referred to as environmental gradients) and obtained over a period of 4 years.  The impact of environmental gradients on the community assemblies in AS-WWTPs, partitioned with respect to distances in position on the ecological gradients. Following gradients were considered specifically,: • Influent wastewater characteristics, • Seasonal variations (winter vs. summer) • Treatment process differences (conventional, oxidation ditch, and sequence batch reactor [SBR]) • Reactor sizes (pilot-scale vs. full-scale reactors) • Chemical stresses defined by a higher mortality induced by return activated sludge (RAS) ozonation (RAS-ozonated vs. non-ozonated reactors) • Inter-annual variation and geographical locations.","organism":"wastewater metagenome","data_type":"Metagenome","center_name":"McGill University","submission_date":"2014/08/01 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN02950679","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from wastewater metagenome","8/15/08","Canada","Quebec","Montréal",45.43,-73.16,"confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","named urban infrastructure at sample level",null,"populated place","wastewater trea